466	939,973,1695,1668	466. Summit of a plant of Dogbane, No. 1, with flowers and pods	A leafy branch-tip of Spreading Dogbane with opposite ovate leaves, cymes of small bell-shaped flowers, and a pair of long slender pods pointing out to the right.
467	637,1173,817,1396	467. Flowers, enlarged.	Two bell-shaped flowers on a short stalk, one open and nodding with its lobes curled back, the other still in bud.
468	809,1453,896,1656	468. Flower with the corolla cut away, to show the stamens.	The stamens left standing on the flower's base, their long pointed anthers leaning together into a narrow cone.
469	672,1482,753,1659	469. The stamens taken away, to show the pistils; two ovaries, with their two large stigmas united into one mass.	The pistils alone: two small ovaries side by side at the bottom, joined above by a single large oval stigma.
470	831,969,933,1396 - 893,1370,934,1397	470. A seed, with its tuft of long hairs or down at one end.	A small oblong seed at the bottom with a long tuft of fine straight hairs rising from its top end.
